# Live suites against the isolated clean-room environment, re-run in full on 2026-10-06 (synthetic data)

Run: `python3 scripts/deploy_snowflake.py --profile cleanroom --suffix CR2 --apply --step test`, as the owner role and then as the application role, against the clean-room environment only
(`FIU_COPILOT_CR2`; the production database was not touched). This is the re-run that `live_suites.log` says was not done after the stale seeding constant in `tests/test_skills_smoke.py` was corrected.
The earlier log is kept unchanged.

RESULT: owner role **19 passed, 1 skipped**; application role **18 passed, 1 skipped, 1 deselected**; no failures; exit 0.
The skipped test is the audit-export one (the optional deletion witness is not provisioned, so it skips). The deselected one is the tamper test that needs the owner role by design.
These suites write inside a transaction and roll back; they assert that no row is left behind. Interpreter: Python 3.14.3, pytest 9.1.1.
What this does not show: the production database `FIU_COPILOT`, which these suites were not run against; and what Snowsight renders.
Local paths are replaced with <repo>, <tmp> and <scratch>; nothing else is changed.

